signature:
Lost-wallet plan. The user marks which cards are "In my wallet" and types the "If lost, call" number from the back of each card. When the wallet goes missing, one visible home-screen button starts a plan:
- every carried card, ordered by urgency (payment, then ID, then health and insurance, then access, then the rest), showing the last 4 digits only;
- the user's saved number with Copy (and Call if url_launcher can be added);
- timestamped steps: Called, Frozen, Cancelled, Replacement ordered, Found it, plus reference numbers;
- progress, and a shareable or copyable lost-wallet report for police, insurer or bank (never a full number or secret);
- plans persist encrypted in the vault, keep a history, and work fully offline.
None of the competitor descriptions checked through the iTunes API (Texode Secure Card Manager, My Card Wallet, Holder, Card Holder, CardStar, 1Password, Bitwarden, Document Expiry) offers this. Their behaviour beyond the descriptions is not verified.
